The animation will feature a unit circle on the left side of the screen, with a point moving continuously along its circumference. Simultaneously, on the right side of the screen, the graph of y = sin(x) will be drawn, synchronized with the point's movement. As the point completes one full rotation around the unit circle, the sine wave will be fully drawn, illustrating the direct relationship between the angle of the point on the circle and the corresponding point on the sine wave graph.
</final_translation>
